# Copilot Instructions

## Project Guidelines
- User prefers explanatory comments in code changes to help understand the implementation.
- Camera left/right movement and pivot transformations must remain non-inverted: if the user drags or moves left, the editor should respond left, and if right, respond right. Note that right-click camera look is expected to follow this non-inverted behavior, as the user corrected that it was previously inverted.
- The real ImGuizmo pivot should be shown and used for transformations when available.
- The editor gizmo should behave like a standard Unreal/CryEngine-style pivot with X/Y/Z and multi-axis plane handles facing the camera.
- The editor gizmo should use a Z-up convention with the blue axis representing Z/up, and gizmo movement should remain non-inverted along the dragged axis.